          ],
          "content": "74"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.485,
            0.09,
            0.626,
            0.112
          ],
          "content": "Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.131,
            0.881,
            0.153
          ],
          "content": "A magnet has two poles—the North pole and the South pole."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.157,
            0.882,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": " The poles of a magnet always exist in pairs. A single North pole or a single South pole cannot exist."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.201,
            0.882,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "Magnetic materials are the materials that are attracted towards a magnet."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.245,
            0.882,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "Non-magnetic materials are the materials that are not attracted towards a magnet."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.289,
            0.882,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": "A freely suspended magnet rests along the north-south direction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.333,
            0.882,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": " The needle of a magnetic compass indicates the north-south direction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.377,
            0.882,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": " When two magnets are brought close to each other, like poles (North-North, South-South) repel each other while unlike poles (North-South) attract each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.335,
            0.489,
            0.74,
            0.514
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Let us enhance our learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.751,
            0.45,
            0.875,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
