          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1. Fill in the blanks"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.573,
            0.881,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": "(i) Unlike poles of two magnets each other, whereas like poles each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.302,
            0.612,
            0.882,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "(ii) The materials that are attracted towards a magnet are called"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.652,
            0.882,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": "(iii) The needle of a magnetic compass rests along the direction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.695,
            0.761,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "(iv) A magnet always has poles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.722,
            0.834,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "2. State whether the following statements are True (T) or False (F)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.765,
            0.863,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "(i) A magnet can be broken into pieces to obtain a single pole. [ ]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.302,
            0.804,
            0.862,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Similar poles of a magnet repel each other. [ ]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.826,
            0.863,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Iron filings mostly stick in the middle of a bar magnet when it is brought near them. [ ]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.866,
            0.863,
            0.905
          ],
          "content": "(iv) A freely suspended bar magnet always aligns with the north-south direction. [ ]"
